{"id":"mahabharata-12-050","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":50,"title":"पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 50 · Krishna comforts Yudhishthira","summary":{"en":"Hearing of Rama's deed, Yudhishthira is full of wonder, and Krishna goes on to speak of his own love for Bhishma. He says that Bhishma, who could conquer the three worlds alone, lies on the bed of arrows and will soon pass away.","kn":"ರಾಮನ ಸಾಹಸ ಕೇಳಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಬೆರಗಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಮೇಲಿನ ತನ್ನ ಪ್ರೀತಿಯನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮೂರು ಲೋಕ ಒಬ್ಬನೇ ಗೆಲ್ಲಬಲ್ಲ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಬಾಣಶಯ್ಯೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಮಲಗಿದ್ದಾನೆ, ಶೀಘ್ರದಲ್ಲಿ ಹೋಗುವನೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"राम का कर्म सुनकर युधिष्ठिर विस्मित होते हैं, और कृष्ण भीष्म के प्रति अपना स्नेह बताते हैं। वे कहते हैं कि अकेले तीनों लोकों को जीतने में समर्थ भीष्म बाणशय्या पर लेटे हैं और शीघ्र चले जाएँगे।","te":"రాముని కార్యం విని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ఆశ్చర్యపోతాడు; కృష్ణుడు భీష్మునిపై తన ప్రేమను చెబుతాడు. మూడు లోకాలను ఒంటరిగా గెలవగల భీష్ముడు బాణశయ్యపై ఉన్నాడని, త్వరలో వెళ్తాడని అంటాడు.","ta":"ராமனின் செயலைக் கேட்டு யுதிஷ்டிரர் வியக்க, கண்ணன் பீஷ்மர் மீது தாம் கொண்ட அன்பைக் கூறுகிறார். மூன்று உலகையும் தனியாக வெல்லக்கூடிய பீஷ்மர் அம்புப் படுக்கையில் உள்ளார், விரைவில் மறைவார் என்கிறார்.","ml":"രാമന്റെ പ്രവൃത്തിയെക്കുറിച്ച് കേട്ട യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അദ്ഭുതത്തിൽ നിറയുന്നു; ഭീഷ്മരോടുള്ള തന്റെ സ്നേഹത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് കൃഷ്ണൻ തുടർന്നു പറയുന്നു. ഒറ്റയ്ക്ക് മൂന്നു ലോകങ്ങളെയും കീഴടക്കാൻ കഴിയുന്ന ഭീഷ്മർ അമ്പുകളുടെ ശയ്യയിൽ കിടക്കുന്നുവെന്നും, ഉടൻ ലോകം വിടുമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.50; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो रामस्य तत्कर्म श्रुत्वा राजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nविस्मयं परमं गत्वा प्रत्युवाच जनार्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard of that deed of Rama, King Yudhishthira was filled with great wonder and said to Janardana:"}},{"n":2,"text":"अहो रामस्य वार्ष्णेय शक्रस्येव महात्मनः ।\nविक्रमो येन वसुधा क्रोधान्निःक्षत्रिया कृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ah, Vrishni hero, the prowess of great-souled Rama is like that of Indra, for in his anger he made the earth empty of kshatriyas!"}},{"n":3,"text":"गोभिः समुद्रेण तथा गोलाङ्गूलर्क्षवानरैः ।\nगुप्ता रामभयोद्विग्नाः क्षत्रियाणां कुलोद्वहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Frightened of Rama, the upholders of the warrior lines were hidden away, protected by cows, by the ocean, and by langurs, bears and monkeys."}},{"n":4,"text":"अहो धन्यो हि लोकोऽयं सभाग्याश्च नरा भुवि ।\nयत्र कर्मेदृशं धर्म्यं द्विजेन कृतमच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ah, blessed is this world and fortunate are the men on earth, Achyuta, where a brahmin has done such a righteous deed."}},{"n":5,"text":"तथा यान्तौ तदा तात तावच्युतयुधिष्ठिरौ ।\nजग्मतुर्यत्र गाङ्गेयः शरतल्पगतः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they went on, dear king, Krishna and Yudhishthira came to the place where the lord, Ganga's son Bhishma, lay on his bed of arrows."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततस्ते ददृशुर्भीष्मं शरप्रस्तरशायिनम् ।\nस्वरश्मिजालसंवीतं सायंसूर्यमिवानलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There they saw Bhishma lying on the spread of arrows, wrapped in a web of his own rays like a fire or the evening sun."}},{"n":7,"text":"उपास्यमानं मुनिभिर्देवैरिव शतक्रतुम् ।\nदेशे परमधर्मिष्ठे नदीमोघवतीमनु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sages waited on him as the gods wait on Indra of a hundred sacrifices, in a most sacred spot beside the river Oghavati."}},{"n":8,"text":"दूरादेव तमालोक्य कृष्णो राजा च धर्मराट् ।\nचत्वारः पाण्डवाश्चैव ते च शारद्वतादयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him from afar, Krishna, King Yudhishthira, the four other Pandavas, and Kripa and the others,"}},{"n":9,"text":"अवस्कन्द्याथ वाहेभ्यः संयम्य प्रचलं मनः ।\nएकीकृत्येन्द्रियग्राममुपतस्थुर्महामुनीन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"got down from their chariots, steadied their restless minds, gathered their senses into one, and approached the great sages."}},{"n":10,"text":"अभिवाद्य च गोविन्दः सात्यकिस्ते च कौरवाः ।\nव्यासादींस्तानृषीन्पश्चाद्गाङ्गेयमुपतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Govinda, Satyaki and the Kauravas first greeted Vyasa and the other seers, and afterwards approached Ganga's son."}},{"n":11,"text":"तपोवृद्धिं ततः पृष्ट्वा गाङ्गेयं यदुकौरवाः ।\nपरिवार्य ततः सर्वे निषेदुः पुरुषर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having asked Ganga's son about the growth of his austerity, the Yadavas and Kauravas, those best of men, sat down all around him."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो निशम्य गाङ्गेयं शाम्यमानमिवानलम् ।\nकिंचिद्दीनमना भीष्ममिति होवाच केशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing Ganga's son like a fire dying down, Keshava, his mind a little saddened, spoke to Bhishma thus:"}},{"n":13,"text":"कच्चिज्ज्ञानानि ते राजन्प्रसन्नानि यथा पुरा ।\nकच्चिदव्याकुला चैव बुद्धिस्ते वदतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, are your faculties of knowledge clear as before? Is your mind free of confusion, best of speakers?"}},{"n":14,"text":"शराभिघातदुःखात्ते कच्चिद्गात्रं न दूयते ।\nमानसादपि दुःखाद्धि शारीरं बलवत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Does your body not ache from the pain of the arrow-blows? Bodily suffering is indeed stronger than suffering of the mind."}},{"n":15,"text":"वरदानात्पितुः कामं छन्दमृत्युरसि प्रभो ।\nशंतनोर्धर्मशीलस्य न त्वेतच्छमकारणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your father's boon you die at will, lord, and your father Shantanu was devoted to dharma; but this is no cause for peace."}},{"n":16,"text":"सुसूक्ष्मोऽपीह देहे वै शल्यो जनयते रुजम् ।\nकिं पुनः शरसंघातैश्चितस्य तव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a very tiny splinter lodged in the body causes pain here; what then of you, pierced by masses of arrows, descendant of Bharata?"}},{"n":17,"text":"कामं नैतत्तवाख्येयं प्राणिनां प्रभवाप्ययौ ।\nभवान्ह्युपदिशेच्छ्रेयो देवानामपि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Truly I ought not to tell you of the origin and dissolution of beings, for you could teach what is best even to the gods."}},{"n":18,"text":"यद्धि भूतं भविष्यच्च भवच्च पुरुषर्षभ ।\nसर्वं तज्ज्ञानवृद्धस्य तव पाणाविवाहितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever has been, will be and is, best of men, all of it lies in your hand like a fruit, since you are ripe in knowledge."}},{"n":19,"text":"संसारश्चैव भूतानां धर्मस्य च फलोदयः ।\nविदितस्ते महाप्राज्ञ त्वं हि ब्रह्ममयो निधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The cycle of rebirth of creatures and the rising of the fruit of dharma are known to you, greatly wise one, for you are a treasury made of Brahman."}},{"n":20,"text":"त्वां हि राज्ये स्थितं स्फीते समग्राङ्गमरोगिणम् ।\nस्त्रीसहस्रैः परिवृतं पश्यामीहोर्ध्वरेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I used to see you ruling a prosperous kingdom, whole in body, free of illness, surrounded by thousands of women, yet keeping your vow of chastity."}},{"n":21,"text":"ऋते शांतनवाद्भीष्मात्त्रिषु लोकेषु पार्थिव ।\nसत्यसंधान्महावीर्याच्छूराद्धर्मैकतत्परात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Except for Bhishma, son of Shantanu, truthful, mighty, heroic and wholly devoted to dharma, king, in the three worlds,"}},{"n":22,"text":"मृत्युमावार्य तरसा शरप्रस्तरशायिनः ।\nनिसर्गप्रभवं किंचिन्न च तातानुशुश्रुम ॥","meaning":{"en":"we have heard of no one else who held back death by force while lying on a bed of arrows, as a power born of his own nature."}},{"n":23,"text":"सत्ये तपसि दाने च यज्ञाधिकरणे तथा ।\nधनुर्वेदे च वेदे च नित्यं चैवान्ववेक्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"In truth, in austerity, in giving, in the conduct of sacrifice, in the science of the bow and in the Veda, and always in careful attention,"}},{"n":24,"text":"अनृशंसं शुचिं दान्तं सर्वभूतहिते रतम् ।\nमहारथं त्वत्सदृशं न कंचिदनुशुश्रुम ॥","meaning":{"en":"gentle, pure, self-controlled, devoted to the good of all beings, a great chariot-warrior: we have heard of no one like you."}},{"n":25,"text":"त्वं हि देवान्सगन्धर्वान्ससुरासुरराक्षसान् ।\nशक्त एकरथेनैव विजेतुं नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For you alone, on a single chariot, could conquer the gods, gandharvas, asuras and rakshasas together; there is no doubt of it."}},{"n":26,"text":"त्वं हि भीष्म महाबाहो वसूनां वासवोपमः ।\nनित्यं विप्रैः समाख्यातो नवमोऽनवमो गुणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed Bhishma, among the Vasus you are like Indra; brahmins always call you the ninth, yet in qualities second to none."}},{"n":27,"text":"अहं हि त्वाभिजानामि यस्त्वं पुरुषसत्तम ।\nत्रिदशेष्वपि विख्यातः स्वशक्त्या सुमहाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know who you are, best of men, famed even among the gods for your own great strength."}},{"n":28,"text":"मनुष्येषु मनुष्येन्द्र न दृष्टो न च मे श्रुतः ।\nभवतो यो गुणैस्तुल्यः पृथिव्यां पुरुषः क्वचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of men, among men I have neither seen nor heard of anyone anywhere on earth equal to you in virtues."}},{"n":29,"text":"त्वं हि सर्वैर्गुणै राजन्देवानप्यतिरिच्यसे ।\nतपसा हि भवाञ्शक्तः स्रष्टुं लोकांश्चराचरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, you surpass even the gods in every virtue, and by your austerity you are able to create the worlds, moving and unmoving."}},{"n":30,"text":"तदस्य तप्यमानस्य ज्ञातीनां संक्षयेण वै ।\nज्येष्ठस्य पाण्डुपुत्रस्य शोकं भीष्म व्यपानुद ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, Bhishma, remove the grief of Pandu's eldest son, who is burning with sorrow over the destruction of his kinsmen."}},{"n":31,"text":"ये हि धर्माः समाख्याताश्चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य भारत ।\nचातुराश्रम्यसंसृष्टास्ते सर्वे विदितास्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The duties declared for the four classes, together with those of the four stages of life, are all known to you, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":32,"text":"चातुर्वेद्ये च ये प्रोक्ताश्चातुर्होत्रे च भारत ।\nसांख्ये योगे च नियता ये च धर्माः सनातनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those taught in the fourfold Veda and the fourfold priestly office, and the eternal duties fixed in Sankhya and Yoga, are also known to you."}},{"n":33,"text":"चातुर्वर्ण्येन यश्चैको धर्मो न स्म विरुध्यते ।\nसेव्यमानः स चैवाद्यो गाङ्गेय विदितस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the one primal dharma that never conflicts with the duties of the four classes when practised is known to you, son of Ganga."}},{"n":34,"text":"इतिहासपुराणं च कार्त्स्न्येन विदितं तव ।\nधर्मशास्त्रं च सकलं नित्यं मनसि ते स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know the Itihasas and Puranas in full, and the whole Dharmashastra is ever present in your mind."}},{"n":35,"text":"ये च केचन लोकेऽस्मिन्नर्थाः संशयकारकाः ।\nतेषां छेत्ता नास्ति लोके त्वदन्यः पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever doubt-raising matters there are in this world, best of men, there is no one but you to cut them away."}},{"n":36,"text":"स पाण्डवेयस्य मनःसमुत्थितं\nनरेन्द्र शोकं व्यपकर्ष मेधया ।\nभवद्विधा ह्युत्तमबुद्धिविस्तरा\nविमुह्यमानस्य जनस्य शान्तये ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, lord of men, draw out by your wisdom the grief that has risen in the mind of the Pandava; for people of your kind, with vast and excellent understanding, exist to bring peace to the bewildered."}}]}]}